The issue: we need to find the minimum unused wire length. We know the total length is M, which we can't waste. We need to minimize this length, so let's start with the longest length possible. Then, we'll alternate placing soldiers to connect them.

So, if N soldiers are placed in spots P, we'll need (N - 1) soldiers’ lengths to connect them:
X, P[0], P[1] + X, P[2], P[3] + X, ... , P[N-2], P[N-1] + X

Above sum is the (N - 1) multiplications of soldier’s wire length from left to right, so without algebra we can say that soldier’s wire length from left to right MUST BE larger than:
x = ((N - 1)*X)/2 + X
x = X*(N + 1)/2

So our used wire length is: M - x. (Note that with N being even, if the used wire length comes out to be less than zero then that's just an edge case that never occurs in this problem.)
</reasoning>

